<%# One work in a list. Rendered by the archive (/days) and by a reader's
    collection (/collection), which are the same object seen twice: a work, a
    date, a recognition mark.

    Locals:
      painting:  the work
      pick:      its day, or nil when the curator removed the day out from under
                 a kept work. A nil pick is the only unlinked row.
      current:   the pick the front door is showing, so a link never points at a
                 URL that immediately 301s (see ApplicationHelper#day_link_path)
      eager:     load the thumbnail eagerly (the first few rows only)
      remove:    render a Remove control. Only ever true on an unlinked row —
                 nesting a button inside the row's own <a> would be an
                 accessibility defect, and an orphan is the one row whose owner
                 has no other way to let it go.

    The whole row is one link, and its accessible name carries date, title and
    artist: a list of bare titles is useless to somebody navigating by link.
    `size: 240` and not the original — ISSUE-001 (commit 2da2f7a) shipped
    full-size JPEGs into 112px boxes once already. %>
<% remove = false unless defined?(remove) %>
<li class="days__day">
  <% if pick %>
    <a class="days__link" href="<%= day_link_path(pick, current) %>"
       aria-label="<%= pick.scheduled_on.to_fs(:daily_long) %>: <%= painting.title %>, <%= painting.artist_display %>">
      <%= render "days/row_body", painting: painting, pick: pick, current: current, eager: eager %>
    </a>
  <% else %>
    <div class="days__link days__link--gone">
      <%= render "days/row_body", painting: painting, pick: nil, current: current, eager: eager %>
    </div>

    <% if remove %>
      <%= button_to "Remove", favorite_path(painting), method: :delete,
            class: "caps-link days__remove",
            form: { class: "days__remove-form" },
            aria: { label: "Remove #{painting.title} from your collection" } %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</li>
